    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538">

                <pb facs="0603" n="499" xml:id="pg499"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 422.11G93/696.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of Ecuador to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-10-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 28, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At our interview of the 14th I assured Mr. Moore that the phrase “juicio final”
                    used in my note of August 8 meant unappealable judgment. I received yesterday
                    from my Government a cablegram that says: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Congress empowers Executive to accept unappealable award.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Every difficulty being removed, I expect of your excellency’s justice that you
                    will deign to direct that Judge Miller perform the duties of the office he has
                    accepted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister of Ecuador.</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
